00:32:06.470 --> 00:32:06.970
a little while ago

00:32:06.970 --> 00:32:07.590
I haven't heard anything

00:32:07.590 --> 00:32:08.470
oh Scott

00:32:08.470 --> 00:32:09.030
Harold

00:32:09.030 --> 00:32:09.880
thank God

00:32:09.880 --> 00:32:11.470
he's stable

00:32:11.470 --> 00:32:12.970
but he's got a subdural

00:32:12.970 --> 00:32:14.950
and the CT scan shows

00:32:14.950 --> 00:32:16.190
increased endocranial pressure

00:32:16.190 --> 00:32:16.810
we're worried about

00:32:16.810 --> 00:32:17.770
a possible herniation

00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:18.610
is he intubated?

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:19.350
yes

00:32:19.350 --> 00:32:20.130
what does that mean?

00:32:20.540 --> 00:32:21.580
it means he can't breathe

00:32:21.580 --> 00:32:22.100
on his own

00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:23.590
if we don't find a way

00:32:23.590 --> 00:32:24.350
to relieve the pressure

00:32:24.350 --> 00:32:25.550
he could bleed out

00:32:25.550 --> 00:32:26.130
and die

00:32:26.130 --> 00:32:27.830
I should get inside

00:32:27.830 --> 00:32:28.470
yes go

00:32:28.470 --> 00:32:29.510
thank you Scott

00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:35.480
Now what?

00:33:03.360 --> 00:33:06.020
Every turn that takes me home

00:33:06.020 --> 00:33:09.950
I imagined you were

00:33:31.820 --> 00:33:57.700
Morning there. Where's your dad?

00:33:57.700 --> 00:34:00.000
He had to go to the hospital.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.000
I'm going to go to the hospital to see someone.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.210
Does he always leave you alone like this?

00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:05.210
I'm not alone.

00:34:05.210 --> 00:34:08.450
He said you'd make pretty good pancakes, but I didn't want to wake you up.

00:34:08.450 --> 00:34:09.650
What are you doing?

00:34:09.650 --> 00:34:10.630
Working on my bat mitzvah.

00:34:10.630 --> 00:34:11.470
You're what now?

00:34:11.470 --> 00:34:14.690
It's a Jewish rite of passage where I become a woman.

00:34:14.690 --> 00:34:17.510
Your father's not Jewish.

00:34:17.510 --> 00:34:19.590
I know, but Mom was.

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:21.830
He tries pretty hard.

00:34:21.830 --> 00:34:24.800
He got me this coach, except he's called a canter and he's letting me have this big party.

00:34:24.800 --> 00:34:26.720
Of course, he wants to plan the whole thing.

00:34:26.720 --> 00:34:28.640
Your father wants to plan a party?

00:34:28.640 --> 00:34:30.000
Yeah.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:30.860
Why?

00:34:30.860 --> 00:34:33.210
I didn't realize he got so involved.

00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:36.510
I remember him as always being away a lot.

00:34:36.510 --> 00:34:37.580
Usually at work.

00:34:37.580 --> 00:34:38.580
I guess.

00:34:38.580 --> 00:34:42.170
But Mom's not around anymore, so he doesn't have much of a choice.

00:34:42.170 --> 00:34:44.280
We're very needy.

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:45.820
Is that so?

00:34:45.820 --> 00:34:47.630
Ephraim was way worse than me.

00:34:47.630 --> 00:34:50.820
They're okay now, but last year wasn't pretty.

00:34:50.820 --> 00:34:52.830
I don't know.

00:34:52.830 --> 00:34:54.570
You guys look pretty happy to me.

00:34:54.570 --> 00:34:56.400
We do okay.

00:34:56.400 --> 00:34:58.410
Oh, those are terrible pictures.

00:34:58.410 --> 00:35:00.000
I got better ones.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.590
- Mm-hmm.

00:35:01.590 --> 00:35:04.560
- Are the ones I want to use for my video slideshow.

00:35:04.560 --> 00:35:06.770
- You're getting a slideshow, huh?

00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:08.570
- I had to study a whole new language for this thing.

00:35:08.570 --> 00:35:17.410
I deserved some stuff.

00:35:17.410 --> 00:35:19.800
- There you are.

00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:25.420
I've been looking everywhere.

00:35:25.420 --> 00:35:29.670
- I thought I'd spend so much time in a hospital again for this.

00:35:30.250 --> 00:35:33.540
Sweetheart, he's going to be okay.

00:35:34.420 --> 00:35:36.710
I need to tell you something, Harold.

00:35:36.750 --> 00:35:37.890
I should have told you sooner.

00:35:38.090 --> 00:35:38.670
No, no, wait.

00:35:39.290 --> 00:35:42.820
First, let me tell you, I got a call from Dr. Chow.

00:35:42.900 --> 00:35:45.910
She says your report came back, your scan is clean.

00:35:50.380 --> 00:35:52.380
It means that you're officially in remission.

00:35:55.230 --> 00:35:59.940
You know, it's impossible to take this in right now, but Rose, this is wonderful.

00:36:05.370 --> 00:36:12.290
what did you need to tell me? Harold Rose. What is it? Is he awake? No, they're moving

00:36:12.290 --> 00:36:30.000
him from the ICU. We can see him now. You know, you were right. I wasn't telling you

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:39.690
the whole truth before. I didn't just come here to see my grandchildren. Okay. I had my hip surgery

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:52.130
about two months ago, and I went to your old hospital in New York. I thought it'd be a chance

00:36:52.130 --> 00:36:58.270
to see you again, but you weren't there.

00:37:01.210 --> 00:37:06.310
That's when I found out that you left and about Julia.

00:37:09.570 --> 00:37:11.170
I was real sorry to hear about that.

00:37:11.330 --> 00:37:12.510
You know how much I loved her.

00:37:14.460 --> 00:37:14.840
I do.

00:37:15.690 --> 00:37:17.990
When I heard that she'd been killed,

00:37:19.730 --> 00:37:21.310
I thought it would make this easier.

00:37:22.460 --> 00:37:23.080
Make what easier?

00:37:23.720 --> 00:37:25.080
Coming here, seeing you.

00:37:27.340 --> 00:37:30.000
I figured you'd be so miserable and lonely, you'd...

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:34.220
Take whatever two-bill apology I could come up with and forgive me.

00:37:34.950 --> 00:37:37.090
On the spot for every wrong thing I've ever done.

00:37:39.590 --> 00:37:40.430
But you're not miserable.

00:37:41.660 --> 00:37:42.440
I have my days.

00:37:43.840 --> 00:37:46.000
Yeah, but you're surrounded by people who love you.

00:37:46.820 --> 00:37:48.940
Because you worked for it, like I never did.

00:37:51.210 --> 00:37:54.550
Well, I do understand the impulse to walk away.

00:37:56.450 --> 00:37:58.110
When Julie was alive, I was pretty good at it.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:09.360
and I have a lot more in common than I care to admit. Except you changed. I've made a lot of

00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:17.580
mistakes in my life, but you were never one of them. I'm proud of what you've done here,

00:38:17.580 --> 00:38:23.800
and it just makes me realize how much I've let you down over the years. I'm sorry.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:37.840
reason you came here is to apologize to me? Basically. You're not dying? Yeah, you always

00:38:37.840 --> 00:38:43.890
did have the flair for the dramatic. Well, I am not dying, but if that's what it'll take

00:38:43.890 --> 00:38:48.090
to get a second chance with you, I could run, probably run out there and catch something.

00:38:48.810 --> 00:38:59.780
Maybe it would have been different if I, if I was younger when mom died. Maybe.

00:39:02.140 --> 00:39:05.120
But I had plenty of chances to get back in touch, and I blew it.

00:39:06.100 --> 00:39:06.540
I don't know.

00:39:08.650 --> 00:39:09.710
You're sitting here now, aren't you?

00:39:10.250 --> 00:39:22.010
I miss her every single day, I feel.

00:40:31.660 --> 00:40:35.660
You send me with that look in your eyes

00:40:35.660 --> 00:40:41.190
And pretend that nobody knows

00:40:41.190 --> 00:40:51.470
Or the secret gets out

00:40:51.470 --> 00:40:59.160
Boy, I've been swooning love

00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:06.210
- The mask.
